IMPORT `s121-d9-service`
IMPORT `s121-efg`
IMPORT `s121-whole`

-- Tests for the whole section. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text and the calendar, written beside the assertion, then run.
-- Unless a scenario says otherwise the sale is on 15 March 2026: the 5-year period is 16 March 2021 to 15 March 2026 (1826 days) and 2 years is 730 days.

§ `Fixtures`

`the sale date` MEANS Date 15 3 2026
`owned and used from 2015` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2015), (Date 15 3 2026)
`one year to the sale` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 16 3 2025), (Date 15 3 2026)
`ten years to the sale` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 16 3 2016), (Date 15 3 2026)
`five years to the sale` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 16 3 2021), (Date 15 3 2026)
`a person with no part in the property` MEANS `an individual who only owned and used the property` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
`an owner-occupier since 2015` MEANS `an individual who only owned and used the property` `owned and used from 2015` `owned and used from 2015` EMPTY
`an occupier since 2015 who owns none` MEANS `an individual who only owned and used the property` EMPTY `owned and used from 2015` EMPTY
`an owner-occupier for one year` MEANS `an individual who only owned and used the property` `one year to the sale` `one year to the sale` EMPTY
`an owner-occupier since 2015 who sold another home on 14 March 2025` MEANS `an individual who only owned and used the property` `owned and used from 2015` `owned and used from 2015` (LIST Date 14 3 2025)

§ `Subsection (a) with the limitation of (b)(1)`

-- 1 single owner-occupier since 2015: nothing reduces the exclusion, the limitation is $250,000.
`a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 300,000` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 300000 FALSE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `a person with no part in the property` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 300,000` EQUALS JUST 250000
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain that stays in gross income` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 300,000` EQUALS JUST 50000
#ASSERT count (`s 121 what stops or reduces the exclusion` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 300,000`) EQUALS 1
`a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 100,000` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 100000 FALSE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `a person with no part in the property` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 100,000` EQUALS JUST 100000
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain that stays in gross income` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 100,000` EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT count (`s 121 what stops or reduces the exclusion` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 100,000`) EQUALS 0
-- exactly at the limitation
`a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 250,000` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 250000 FALSE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `a person with no part in the property` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 250,000` EQUALS JUST 250000
-- one dollar over
`a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 250,001` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 250001 FALSE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `a person with no part in the property` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 250,001` EQUALS JUST 250000
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain that stays in gross income` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 250,001` EQUALS JUST 1
-- a loss is not "gain": not covered
`a single owner-occupier selling at a loss` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` (0 MINUS 100) FALSE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `a person with no part in the property` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a single owner-occupier selling at a loss` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the treatment record carries the limitation
#ASSERT (`s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 300,000`)'s `the limitation applied` EQUALS JUST 250000
#ASSERT (`s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` `a single owner-occupier selling at a gain of 300,000`)'s `the requirements of subsection (a) are met, with (d)(1) and (b)(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Joint returns: (d)(1) and (b)(2)`

-- 2 a couple on a joint return, one owner-occupier and one occupier: (b)(2)(A) holds, so the limitation is $500,000.
`a couple, one owning and both using since 2015, gain 600,000` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 600000 TRUE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `an occupier since 2015 who owns none` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a couple, one owning and both using since 2015, gain 600,000` EQUALS JUST 500000
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain that stays in gross income` `a couple, one owning and both using since 2015, gain 600,000` EQUALS JUST 100000
#ASSERT (`s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` `a couple, one owning and both using since 2015, gain 600,000`)'s `the limitation applied` EQUALS JUST 500000
`a couple, one owning and both using since 2015, gain 400,000` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 400000 TRUE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `an occupier since 2015 who owns none` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a couple, one owning and both using since 2015, gain 400,000` EQUALS JUST 400000
-- 3 the spouse used it only 365 days of the 5 years: (b)(2)(A)(ii) fails, so (b)(2)(B): $250,000 for the taxpayer plus $0 for the spouse.
`a spouse who used it for one year only` MEANS `an individual who only owned and used the property` EMPTY `one year to the sale` EMPTY
`a couple, spouse used it one year, gain 600,000` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 600000 TRUE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `a spouse who used it for one year only` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a couple, spouse used it one year, gain 600,000` EQUALS JUST 250000
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain that stays in gross income` `a couple, spouse used it one year, gain 600,000` EQUALS JUST 350000
#ASSERT count (`s 121 what stops or reduces the exclusion` `a couple, spouse used it one year, gain 600,000`) EQUALS 1
-- 4 the spouse sold another home on 14 March 2025, within the 2 years: (b)(2)(A)(iii) fails, so (b)(2)(B): $250,000 plus $0 for the barred spouse.
`a couple, spouse barred by an earlier sale, gain 600,000` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 600000 TRUE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `an owner-occupier since 2015 who sold another home on 14 March 2025` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a couple, spouse barred by an earlier sale, gain 600,000` EQUALS JUST 250000
-- 5 neither spouse meets the requirements and no reason is given: (d)(1) fails, (c) fails: $0, said in the text's own words.
`a couple, each with one year, gain 300,000` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 300000 TRUE `an owner-occupier for one year` `an owner-occupier for one year` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a couple, each with one year, gain 300,000` EQUALS JUST 0
-- the same couple, selling for a change of employment: (c) would apply, but whose periods measure the shorter period on a joint return is not said (fork F17)
`a couple, each with one year, selling for a change of employment` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 300000 TRUE `an owner-occupier for one year` `an owner-occupier for one year` EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a couple, each with one year, selling for a change of employment` EQUALS NOTHING
-- the spouse is an individual to whom section 877(a)(1) applies: what that does to a joint return is not said
`an expatriate spouse` MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF `owned and used from 2015`, `owned and used from 2015`) FALSE (Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY) (Date 1 1 1900) EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE (Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY) FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY TRUE
`a couple, the spouse an expatriate` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 300000 TRUE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `an expatriate spouse` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a couple, the spouse an expatriate` EQUALS NOTHING

