#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain that stays in gross income` `a gain of 200,000 half of it earned while rented` EQUALS JUST 100000
#ASSERT (`s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` `a gain of 200,000 half of it earned while rented`)'s `the gain allocated to periods of nonqualified use` EQUALS JUST 100000
#ASSERT count (`s 121 what stops or reduces the exclusion` `a gain of 200,000 half of it earned while rented`) EQUALS 1
-- 10 the same with depreciation of 40,000 taken in 2018: (d)(6) first takes 40,000 of the gain, then (b)(5) allocates half of the remaining 160,000, which is 80,000; so 80,000 is excluded.
-- (Allocating first, 100,000, and subtracting 40,000 after would give 60,000: that is the order (b)(5)(D)(i) rules out.)
`depreciation of 40,000 taken in 2018` MEANS `Depreciation adjustment` WITH
    `amount` IS 40000
    `period it is attributable to` IS (Span OF (Date 1 1 2018), (Date 31 12 2018))
`a gain of 200,000 with depreciation of 40,000 after May 6, 1997` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 200000 FALSE `an owner of ten years who lived in it for the last five` `a person with no part in the property` (LIST `depreciation of 40,000 taken in 2018`) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a gain of 200,000 with depreciation of 40,000 after May 6, 1997` EQUALS JUST 80000
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain that stays in gross income` `a gain of 200,000 with depreciation of 40,000 after May 6, 1997` EQUALS JUST 120000
#ASSERT (`s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` `a gain of 200,000 with depreciation of 40,000 after May 6, 1997`)'s `the gain to which subsection (d)(6) applies` EQUALS JUST 40000
#ASSERT count (`s 121 what stops or reduces the exclusion` `a gain of 200,000 with depreciation of 40,000 after May 6, 1997`) EQUALS 2
-- a gain of 1,000,000: half allocated, 500,000 left, capped at 250,000
`a gain of 1,000,000 half of it earned while rented` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 1000000 FALSE `an owner of ten years who lived in it for the last five` `a person with no part in the property` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a gain of 1,000,000 half of it earned while rented` EQUALS JUST 250000
#ASSERT count (`s 121 what stops or reduces the exclusion` `a gain of 1,000,000 half of it earned while rented`) EQUALS 2
-- a depreciation adjustment attributable to a period that straddles May 6, 1997 is not covered
`depreciation across May 6, 1997` MEANS `Depreciation adjustment` WITH
    `amount` IS 40000
    `period it is attributable to` IS (Span OF (Date 1 1 1997), (Date 31 12 1997))
`a gain with depreciation across May 6, 1997` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 200000 FALSE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `a person with no part in the property` (LIST `depreciation across May 6, 1997`) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a gain with depreciation across May 6, 1997` EQUALS NOTHING
-- depreciation taken in 1996 does not count: all of the gain is excluded
`depreciation taken in 1996` MEANS `Depreciation adjustment` WITH
    `amount` IS 40000
    `period it is attributable to` IS (Span OF (Date 1 1 1996), (Date 31 12 1996))
`a gain with depreciation taken in 1996` MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` `the sale date` 200000 FALSE `an owner-occupier since 2015` `a person with no part in the property` (LIST `depreciation taken in 1996`) FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `a gain with depreciation taken in 1996` EQUALS JUST 200000

