#ASSERT `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` `no joint return, the spouse states no service` EQUALS JUST 0

-- 21 (b)(5)(C)(ii)(II): "the taxpayer or the taxpayer's spouse is serving on qualified official extended duty" exempts those days from nonqualified use, on a return that is not joint as on one that is.
-- Sale on 15 March 2026. The taxpayer owned the home from 1 January 2010 to the sale (16 years of 2010 to 2025 are 16 x 365 + 4 leap days = 5844 days, and 1 January to 15 March 2026 is 74: 5918 days)
-- and lived in it from 1 January 2010 to 31 December 2011 and from 1 January 2024 to the sale (805 days in the 5-year period, so (a) is met). The days owned and not lived in are 1 January 2012 to 31 December 2023: 12 years with 3 leap days, 4383 days.
-- The spouse served from 1 January 2014 to 31 December 2022: 9 years with 2 leap days, 3287 days, inside the cap of 10 years. So the nonqualified days are 4383 - 3287 = 1096 (2012: 366, 2013: 365, 2023: 365); without the spouse's service, 4383.
-- Gain 5918: allocated 5918 x 1096/5918 = 1096, so 4822 is eligible and, being under $250,000, is excluded; without the service 5918 - 4383 = 1535.
`owned from 2010 to the sale` MEANS LIST Span OF (Date 1 1 2010), (Date 15 3 2026)
`used in 2010 and 2011 and from 2024` MEANS LIST
    Span OF (Date 1 1 2010), (Date 31 12 2011)
